      "writtenOn": "2025-02-21T19:21:40Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "These are mostly for convenience to cut down on the number of places/times we make these determinations. For now, I think I would advocate for either keeping them or, if we do remove them, instead opting to simply pass in these bools into key creation helpers.\n\nBasically, `VulkanRenderPassMetaData` exists to more closely mimic future `RenderPassDesc` structure which could provide more granular control over things such as subpass structure. Currently, `RenderPassDesc` data gets taken in by methods responsible for creating indepedent rp keys (like for caching) or adding rp info to existing keys (as a part of a graphics pipeline key), and any necessary info is accumulated into this metadata struct which then gets passed around. So, to remove these bools as member attributes, we could:\n\nA) Pass in `RenderPassDesc` (or just its relevant properties such as dstreadstrategy) along with the `VulkanRenderPassMetaData` we currently pass in to key helpers (`populate_key` which kicks off a cascade of key addition functions), allowing us to make these determinations later and not store them.\n\nB) If we go the route you asked about re: adding input attachments we could add an input attachment to `VulkanRenderPassMetaData::fAttachments` that either consists of the color (in case of dst reads) / the color resolve texture information (in case of loading msaa from resolve), then I think we could examine the load/store op to make determinations. Playing around w/ this some locally, I think it would make sense to go ahead and create + use a `SubpassDesc` struct at least w/ Vulkan to more easily represent how input attachments are used differently in the different subpasses. More work, but seems more future-thinking.\n\nAnyhow, just some intial thoughts before this gets too long. Happy to hop on a call or have a magical hallway convo about it :)",
